[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849488320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3849488320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3849488320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lcofA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-04T20:04:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T20:04:57Z","body":"> It only displays path and edit button for each extension.\r\n> [...]\r\n> There could be a column called \"Name\"\r\n\r\nActually, I think adding a `name = \"...\"` property to .gdextension files is a great idea! I don't know if it needs to be addressed in this PR, but I think we should do it.\r\n\r\nOf course, any GDExtensions that exist now won't have one, though, so we still need a sane fallback if there is no name","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849488320/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849534268","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3849534268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3849534268,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lczs8","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-04T20:15:12Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T20:15:12Z","body":"I think adding a name should be done in a follow-up PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849534268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868772031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3868772031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3868772031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mmMa_","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T01:09:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T11:11:52Z","body":"Maybe I'm too much of a programmer in this, but I would prefer a highlighted text editor to edit `.gdextension` files (with a format checker and errors, ideally) over a UI.\r\n\r\nThe main reason is that there is information in the file that we cannot reasonably represent in an editor UI. For example, currently, you can edit the entry symbol etc., but you cannot edit the linked binaries. If you are making a file from scratch, you cannot use this editor. If you aren't making one from scratch, what use is there to edit it? In that case, you are likely opening a `.gdextension` file made by somebody else for a GDExtension you use, and editing it would be incorrect and break things. There are also potentially comments in the file.\r\n\r\nListing GDExtensions in a tab makes sense to me. I currently provide an empty \"plugin\" file for my GDExtension because people have complained that my GDExtension didn't load because they couldn't see it in the \"plugin\" tab. I'm sure my users aren't the only ones, so listing loaded GDExtensions in a tab should help.\r\n\r\nAnother question, from your screenshot it looks like you'd be editing `.gdextension` files from the settings tab. What happens when you double click the `.gdextension` file?\r\nI'd say that people using the editor tab are more likely to be users than GDExtension authors. I'd expect to be able to edit the `.gdextension` file when i double click it (though notably, this currently reloads the gdextension, so if you were to override that you'd have to add the reload functionality elsewhere).\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868772031/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3869987972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3869987972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3869987972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mq1SE","user":{"login":"ajreckof","id":66184050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTg0MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66184050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof","html_url":"https://github.com/ajreckof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T08:07:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T08:09:00Z","body":"I think we need to better clarify who this is for and what this is for. I think that if you already know how to edit everything directly from the text ffile this is not for you. I feel like this is better perceived as a part of the functionality to create everything from godot's editor. As such, this is more addressed to people who don't have the knowledge. I agree there should be a way to modify the binaries but in a less destructive way then just editing the names and people then complaining that it is not working anymore because they didn't understand that it is not enough and they should also modify the scons file. For example i could see the binaries being linked to the new name property cited before modifying it would also modify in the scons script the libname variable if it exist and modify in the .gdextensions the binaries.\r\n\r\nIf we really want to have binaries being editable directly in the ui it should at least be hidden in a advanced section hidden by default similar to what we have for signal connection or editor settings\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3869987972/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871266392","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871266392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871266392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mvtZY","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T11:51:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T11:51:44Z","body":"@Ivorforce Users who would prefer to edit this file as text can just edit the file in their text editor of choice. That doesn't mean we shouldn't have this dialog. As for \"you cannot edit the linked binaries\", note that the dialogue was more capable in the past, but I was asked to remove the functionality.\r\n\r\n> If you are making a file from scratch, you cannot use this editor. If you aren't making one from scratch, what use is there to edit it?\r\n\r\nThe original context was that you can make a GDExtension from scratch. But aside from that, I think editing *is* useful. Or, at a minimum, opening the editor for the purposes of *viewing* what is there is itself useful.\r\n\r\n> Another question, from your screenshot it looks like you'd be editing .gdextension files from the settings tab. What happens when you double click the .gdextension file? ... I'd expect to be able to edit the .gdextension file when i double click it\r\n\r\nThat's a good idea. I pushed an update to the PR so that it will `OS.shell_open` the .gdextension file.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n@ajreckof Yes, and that's precisely the context in which this was created, as part of a way to view a GDExtension that was just created in the editor UI, and the creation process absolutely should be given a UI.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is honestly getting tiring to go back and forth on this. The scope is either too wide or too narrow for each reviewer that looks at it. This editor was made with the context of creating GDExtensions, then I was asked to separate out the editing from the creation, and now I am being told that this separation results in a useless editor. I completely disagree with all such reviews, I think either of these PRs are useful on their own and I just think these should be merged.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871266392/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871285555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871285555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871285555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mvyEz","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T11:56:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T11:58:39Z","body":"Personally, I do agree that this is a useful addition, and that it stands on its own without https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90979. My main gripe is that I think it would work better as a text editor. This would allow you to edit the file entirely, without loss of data or information.\r\n\r\n> That's a good idea. I pushed an update to the PR so that it will OS.shell_open the .gdextension file.\r\n\r\nWhat does this do? Open it in the default text editor?\r\n\r\nThe 'reload' functionality could probably be put in the `GDExtension` tab :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871285555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871305904","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871305904","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871305904,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mv3Cw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T12:00:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T12:00:49Z","body":"> I think either of these PRs are useful on their own and I just think these should be merged.\r\n\r\nI concur. It looks like there are different expectations on what the dialog should do, but after adding too much features at once will come a suggestion to split the PR into smaller parts and the cycle continues xd\r\nRight now this adds a dialog that lists installed extensions; it's already a functionality that did not exist before. It's fine to expand it in follow-ups, as long as it won't involve completely replacing the code.\r\n\r\n> My main gripe is that I think it would work better as a text editor.\r\n\r\nYou can already text edit a .gdextension file from FileSystem dock.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871305904/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871323893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871323893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871323893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mv7b1","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T12:04:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T12:32:27Z","body":"> > My main gripe is that I think it would work better as a text editor.\r\n> \r\n> You can already text edit a .gdextension file from FileSystem dock.\r\n\r\nI cannot; when I double click the `.gdextension` file in 4.3 through 4.6, it opens it in the inspector as `Resource` and reloads it (e.g. re-shows loading errors if there are any). This is on macOS.\r\n\r\n> Right now this adds a dialog that lists installed extensions; it's already a functionality that did not exist before. It's fine to expand it in follow-ups, as long as it won't involve completely replacing the code.\r\n\r\nThen maybe we should merge the dialogue / tab without the file editor? In context this sounds most uncontroversial. I'd be hesitant to add a file editor I don't think is very useful, especially because I will likely continue advocating using a rich text editor instead of a lossy UI editor in the future.\n\r\nThe settings tab can already serve some interesting functions, such as showing whether the `.gdextension` file loaded correctly, showing the binary that ended up being loaded for the current system from the `.gdextension` file, or showing a button that navigates to the file in the `FileSystem` dock (all acceptable as follow-ups).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871323893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871371718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871371718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871371718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mwHHG","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T12:16:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T12:16:10Z","body":"> I cannot; when I double click the .gdextension file in 4.3 through 4.6, it opens it in the inspector as Resource and reloads it (e.g. re-shows loading errors if there are any). This is on macOS.\r\n\r\nRight-click and Open in External Editor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871371718/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871758874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3871758874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3871758874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mxloa","user":{"login":"Jordyfel","id":76705401,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NzA1NDAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76705401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordyfel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordyfel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T13:37:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:43:21Z","body":"If the consensus is that editing via dialog is not a good idea (no strong opinion myself), then it would make sense to display in the UI, and provide explanatory tooltips, to properties that carry meaningful information to people using a GDExtension, not those developing one.\r\n\r\nThe entry symbol and reloadable toggle aren't such, the compatibility versions are. So to me something like this makes sense:\r\n- No edit dialog\r\n- Compat versions and future user-relevant metadata displayed in the tree table\r\n- Edit shortcut that opens the `.gdextension` file in external editor, pointing people to it (I'm not sure about the current one, I never would have thought to double click the item without reading here)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3871758874/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3872276765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3872276765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3872276765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mzkEd","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T15:05:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T10:57:41Z","body":"> What does this do? Open it in the default text editor?\r\n\r\nOn Windows, the first time, it asks \"How do you want to open this .gdextension file?\". In this dialog I selected VS Code and clicked the \"Always\" button, so now it opens directly in VS Code. So, technically, it's whatever default program you have configured at the OS level to handle a given file type.\r\n\r\n> The 'reload' functionality could probably be put in the GDExtension tab :)\r\n\r\nGreat idea! Added that too (only appears when the extension is reloadable):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1033\" height=\"294\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-02-09 070158\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a343cf05-e560-43c9-b933-ca451a790e1e\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3872276765/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3889892535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115846#issuecomment-3889892535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115846","id":3889892535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7n2wy3","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T10:01:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T10:01:06Z","body":"The same focus problem already exists in plugins tab.","au